WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.159
Stops, scrap and long
start-ups all cost money.

00:00:03.159 --> 00:00:05.408
But the press with the
most visible problem

00:00:05.408 --> 00:00:07.860
is not always the one
with the biggest loss.

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:11.649
The field diagnostic is the
first step of VP Expert.

00:00:11.649 --> 00:00:14.453
A short on-site review
starts with your production

00:00:14.453 --> 00:00:17.202
figures and the people
who know the equipment.

00:00:17.572 --> 00:00:20.157
No new machine connection
is needed for this step.

00:00:20.867 --> 00:00:25.437
Enter the production period, the relevant
costs and the losses for each press.

00:00:25.807 --> 00:00:29.594
Keep unsupported figures separate. A
missing value is a question for the

00:00:29.594 --> 00:00:32.135
visit, not a zero to
use in the calculation.

00:00:32.845 --> 00:00:35.224
Compare the records with what operators,

00:00:35.224 --> 00:00:39.388
maintenance and quality see on the
shop floor. Review the checkpoints,

00:00:39.388 --> 00:00:42.200
note exceptions and
identify recurring problems.

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:47.111
The report brings scrap, stoppages
and set-up losses together in euros.

00:00:47.111 --> 00:00:50.989
This is an example with fictional
figures, not a savings promise.

00:00:51.359 --> 00:00:54.628
Use it to identify the presses
that deserve attention first.

00:00:55.338 --> 00:00:58.893
The handover proposes up to three
priorities: what to do first,

00:00:58.893 --> 00:01:01.334
who owns it and what still needs checking.

00:01:01.704 --> 00:01:05.474
The roadmap stays with the site,
whether or not the work continues.

00:01:06.184 --> 00:01:08.643
Use the quick estimate for a first look.

00:01:08.643 --> 00:01:13.280
Then open VP Expert to investigate the
defects the field review has identified.
